:body.
:h1 id=intro.Introduction
:p.This book is written in :hp2.BookMaster:ehp2. markup and formatted by
:hp1.bookie:ehp1., our own formatter. The markup uses tags such as
&colon.p. and &colon.h1.; a symbol like &amp.colon. gives a colon.
:p.Here is a list of what bookie knows:
:ol.
:li.headings, paragraphs and highlighting;
:li.ordered, unordered and simple lists, nested:
:ul.
:li.like this one,
:li.and this.
:eul.
:li.definition lists, examples, figures and tables.
:eol.
:h2.Definitions
:dl tsize=10.
:dthd.Term
:ddhd.Meaning
:dt.CP
:dd.The Control Program.
:dt.CMS
:dd.The Conversational Monitor System.
:edl.
:h2.An example
:xmp.
/* HELLO EXEC */
SAY 'Hello, world'
.not a control word inside an example
:exmp.
:note.Examples keep their spacing.
:h1.Tables
:table cols='10 20 30'.
:thd.
:row.
:c.Command
:c.Where
:c.What it does
:ethd.
:row.
:c.LXCALL
:c.CMS
:c.Calls a Linux service through the spool bridge.
:row.
:c.TROFF
:c.CMS
:c.Formats a troff document with groff.
:etable.
:p.See :q.Introduction:eq. for the beginning.
:euserdoc.
